parallel_group.prompt:
Deliver a CLI seat's prompt by FILE instead of by pipe, and let the caller choose the temp root.

FILES YOU OWN (touch no others): src/kbutillib/domains/ai/llm/apis/cli_common.py and tests/domains/ai/council/test_cli_backends.py.

THE BUG, MEASURED. run_cli (around line 698) currently feeds the child with `await proc.communicate(stdin_text.encode('utf-8'))` (around line 762). The parent therefore pumps a pipe from the same asyncio event loop that also performs synchronous store I/O. When that loop stalls, the child gives up waiting for its prompt and exits with 'Input must be provided through stdin'. On a 19,276-item production run this destroyed 23 of 24 Claude attempts, reported as generic transport failures.

WHAT TO BUILD.
1. Write the prompt text to a file INSIDE the existing per-call TemporaryDirectory (created around line 743) and hand the child `stdin=<that file opened for reading>` instead of a PIPE. The child's view must not change -- it still reads its prompt on stdin, which is the documented spelling the installed CLIs expect. Because the file lives in the per-call temp directory it is removed with it, so the prompt never persists; keep that property.
2. Add an optional `temp_root` parameter to run_cli, passed through to tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(dir=...). When None, preserve today's default. Do NOT add a config field or read config here -- config is owned by another task and the wiring by a third; your job ends at the parameter.
3. Still capture stderr and stdout as today, still honour the timeout, and still kill the child PROCESS GROUP on timeout and reap it -- that behaviour is load-bearing for the daemon's bounded drain and must not regress.

DO NOT TOUCH the argv construction in llm/apis/cli.py. In particular `--tools ""`, `--system-prompt`, `--no-session-persistence` and the deliberate ABSENCE of `--bare` and `--dangerously-skip-permissions` must all stay exactly as they are: `--bare` would move the call onto metered API billing and defeat the purpose of a CLI seat.

TESTS. Extend test_cli_backends.py, keeping its existing assertions intact -- they assert the argv flag by flag and are the one test standing between a CLI seat and metered billing.
- the child receives the full prompt text (use a fake executable that echoes its stdin back);
- the prompt NEVER appears in argv;
- the prompt file does not exist after run_cli returns;
- a temp_root argument places the working directory under that root;
- a child that exits without reading stdin does not hang the parent and does not raise a BrokenPipeError out of run_cli;
- the timeout path still kills the process group.

Background reference, possibly unreachable from your worktree: agent-io/prds/council-per-seat-queues-v1/fullprompt.md on branch wip, section 'CLI transport corrections'.
